@startuml
!include https://static.visual-paradigm.com/web/resources/plantuml-stdlib/themes/vp.puml
title Reset Password Sequence Diagram

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor black
    LifeLineBorderColor #555555
    LifeLineBackgroundColor white
    ActivationBorderColor #333333
    ActivationBackgroundColor #70C5E8
}

actor "Guest" as A
boundary "Spring Security" as SEC
control "AuthController" as CT
control "PasswordResetService" as SV
entity "UserRepository" as REPO
entity "PasswordResetCodeRepository" as CODES
control "EmailService" as MAIL
control "RefreshTokenService" as TOKENS
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

autonumber

A -> SEC: POST /api/v1/auth/password/forgot, POST /api/v1/auth/password/reset
activate SEC
note over SEC
public route, no token required
end note
SEC -> CT: Forward the request
deactivate SEC
activate CT
CT -> SV: sendResetCode(request), then resetPassword(request)
activate SV
alt Request succeeds
note over A,SV
Step 1 is POST /auth/password/forgot, which always answers 200
end note
SV -> REPO: Find the enabled user by email
SV -> CODES: Check cooldown and hourly limit
SV -> CODES: Invalidate old codes and save the new BCrypt hash
CODES -> DB: UPDATE and INSERT password_reset_codes
SV -> MAIL: Send the code (a mail failure is only logged)
note over A,SV
Step 2 is POST /auth/password/reset
end note
SV -> CODES: Load the latest unused code and compare
SV -> REPO: Set the new password hash
REPO -> DB: UPDATE users
SV -> TOKENS: Revoke all refresh tokens
TOKENS -> DB: UPDATE refresh_tokens
SV --> CT: Use-case result
CT --> SEC: 200 OK ApiResponse<Void>
SEC --> A: 200 OK ApiResponse<Void>
else Invalid body, or the code is wrong, expired, used or out of attempts
SV --> CT: BusinessException
CT --> SEC: 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
SEC --> A: 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
end

@enduml
